      "title": "Problem: The Mirror Number",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": true,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "using System;\n\nclass Program\n{\n    static int ReverseNumber(int n)\n    {\n        int rev = 0;\n\n        while (n > 0)\n        {\n            rev = rev * 10 + n % 10;\n            n /= 10;\n        }\n\n        return rev;\n    }\n\n    static bool IsPalindrome(int n)\n    {\n        return n == ReverseNumber(n);\n    }\n\n    static void Main()\n    {\n        int N = int.Parse(Console.ReadLine());\n\n        int reversed = ReverseNumber(N);\n\n        if (reversed != N && IsPalindrome(N + reversed))\n            Console.WriteLine(\"YES\");\n        else\n            Console.WriteLine(\"NO\");\n    }\n}",
      "statement": "A number is called a “mirror number” if:\n\nReversing its digits produces a number different from the original.\nThe sum of the original number and its reversed number is a palindrome.\n\nYour task is to determine whether a given number N is a mirror number.",
